{
  "mcpInstructions": [
    "Read @xh/hoist-chat-kit/docs/README.md before you build a chat, assistant, or other LLM feature.",
    "Build a conversation on ChatModel and render it with chatPanel or chatWorkspace. Do not hand-roll message lists, composers, or turn state.",
    "Stream replies through a kit transport and codec. Do not parse SSE or NDJSON streams by hand.",
    "Call a backend from the browser when it takes the user's OAuth token. Relay it through the Hoist server when it needs a secret API key, as a model provider does. The kit supports both equally - see @xh/hoist-chat-kit/transport/README.md 'Choose where requests go'. Never put a secret API key in the browser.",
    "Render model output with chatMarkdown, not Hoist's markdown. It renders half-written syntax cleanly as text streams, and it blocks raw HTML and images by default.",
    "Show app components in a reply through a ChatUiCatalog. Do not parse model text for UI.",
    "Import from the package barrels, such as @xh/hoist-chat-kit/core and @xh/hoist-chat-kit/desktop/cmp/chat. Never import from impl folders.",
    "The kit has desktop components only."
  ],
  "mcpCategories": [
    {"id": "package", "title": "Package Documentation"},
    {"id": "concept", "title": "Concept Documentation"},
    {"id": "conventions", "title": "Conventions"},
